  "created": "2026-09-19T17:16:29.123Z",
  "description": "Tracks the errors real visitors actually hit - 404s, 500s, TLS and DNS failures - by asking their browsers to report them through Network Error Logging, then shows them on three Settings dashboards and emails subscribed users when a site's error volume goes abnormal. Server logs record what the server thinks it served; NEL moves the observation point into the browser, so it also catches certificate problems, connection resets and failures on assets served from a CDN. Note that NEL is Chromium-only, so every figure is a lower bound rather than a count.",
